    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-73569",
      "knowledge_point_id": "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination",
      "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      "worked_solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+2z=1 \\\\  & y-3z=-9 \\\\  & z=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-3(1)=-9\\,⟹\\,y=-6.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-6$ and $z=1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-(-6)+2(1)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-7,y=-6$, and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-7,-6,1⟩.$",
